HELP = """Render phone cards (PNG) for Sylvester Chatwell.

Usage: recipe-card <spec.json> [--out <file.png>]
       recipe-card --which-chrome     print the Chrome binary that will be used
       recipe-card --help

Without --out the PNG is written next to the spec with the spec's name
(dinner.json -> dinner.png). Prints the absolute PNG path.

Card kinds (chosen by "kind"; without it a spec with "days" is a meal plan,
otherwise a recipe):

  recipe  title, ingredient list (+ tools), then a Cooking For Engineers grid
  plan    weekly meal plan: one block per day, offers, saving, staples, total
  week    week overview (calendar events + dinner per day), dark theme
  steps   portrait share card (1080 x 1920 px): numbered steps + bonus step

Every spec may set:
  "lang":   "da" (default) or "en" - the language of every fixed text on the
            card (headings, chips, footer words, weekday/month abbreviations)
            and of the hyphenation used in narrow columns.
  "labels": {key: text} overriding any built-in label of that language; the
            list keys (weekdays, weekday_abbr, months) take lists of 7/7/12.
            Keys and their defaults are listed at the end of --help.

Recipe spec:
{
  "title": "Meatballs in cream sauce",
  "subtitle": "4 servings · 45 min",                   optional
  "start": ["Preheat oven: 200 °C fan"],               optional: before any step
  "tools": ["Frying pan", "Pot"],                      optional: equipment
  "recipe": {                                          the final step
    "do": "Turn the meatballs in the sauce",
    "with": [                                          what this step combines
      {"do": "Mix, shape 30 balls",
       "with": [{"amount": "1 kg", "name": "minced pork"},
                {"amount": "2", "name": "eggs"}]},
      {"amount": "5 dl", "name": "whipping cream"}
    ]
  },
  "notes": ["Can be made the day before."]             optional
}
An ingredient is {"amount": ..., "name": ...} (amount shown bold) or a plain
string. "\\n" in a step text forces a line break. Each step spans exactly the
rows it combines; time runs left to right. Limits: title 48, subtitle 40,
ingredient name 28, amount 8, tool 26, start line 40 chars; max 18
ingredients, 8 tools, 3 start lines, 5 steps in a row.

Meal-plan spec ("kind": "plan" optional):
{
  "title": "Week 42",
  "subtitle": "12-16 October · delivery Monday 07-09",  optional
  "days": [                                             1-7 days
    {"day": "Monday", "date": "12/10", "dish": "Salmon with lemon butter",
     "details": "Fried courgette", "offer": "salmon -26%", "time": "30 min"},
    {"day": "Friday", "dish": "Taco Friday", "highlight": true,
     "items": ["Spiced beef", "Guacamole and cheddar"]}
  ],
  "footer": {"saving": "approx. 370 kr", "total": "approx. 1,950 kr",   optional
             "staples": [{"amount": "30", "name": "eggs"}, "coffee"],
             "note": "..."}
}
Day keys: day (required), dish (required), date, details, offer, time,
items, highlight. Limits: title 40, subtitle 60, day 10, date 8, dish 60,
details 90, offer 34, time 12, item 44, staple 24, staple amount 10, saving
20, total 20, note 70 chars; max 4 items per day, 10 staples.

Week spec ("kind": "week"):
{
  "kind": "week", "title": "Week 43", "subtitle": "19-25 October",
  "note": "Clocks go back on Sunday",                   optional
  "days": [{"day": "Monday", "date": "19/10",
            "events": [{"time": "17:30", "title": "Running club", "who": "Sam"}],
            "dinner": "Salmon with lemon butter"}]
}
"date" is day/month; the month is shown abbreviated. Events: title
(required), time (missing = all-day label), who. Limits: title 30, subtitle
40, day 10, date 6, time 11, event 42, who 12, dinner 44, note 70 chars; max
6 events per day.

Steps spec ("kind": "steps"):
{
  "kind": "steps", "title": "Sylvester Chatwell",
  "subtitle": "Your household butler in Grok Bot",     optional
  "kicker": "Get started",                             optional (default: label steps_kicker)
  "steps": [{"title": "Get Grok Premium", "detail": "Includes Grok Bot"}],  1-7 steps
  "bonus": {"title": "Ask for a recipe card", "detail": "..."},             optional
  "footer": "github.com/you/repo"                      optional
}
Limits: title 32, subtitle 50, kicker 30, step title 40, detail 110,
footer 60 chars.

Fonts come from the repo's fonts/ folder (embedded into the page), so cards
look the same on every machine. Chrome: $RECIPE_CARD_CHROME, else
<repo>/.deps/chrome/chrome, else google-chrome, google-chrome-stable,
chromium, chromium-browser on PATH, else Google Chrome.app on macOS.

The laid-out card is measured in Chrome; if a cell spills over its edge or a
step goes one-word-per-line, the card gets denser (smaller fonts, tighter
rows) until it fits.

Exit 0 = ok, 64 = invalid spec or limit exceeded, 65 = still doesn't fit (the
message names the texts to shorten), 1 = rendering failed (no Chrome, font
missing, Chrome error).
